# What happens to the output of one block, and where the hole was before assertions existed.

title What is checked about what a block printed

box run 280 60 440 80 "One block, one run" "It printed something. Here is what" "the build does with it."

box stored 40 190 440 140 "capture=stdout" "The output goes into expected/<id>.txt" "and the page quotes it. One changed" "byte fails the build, on all four" "platforms."

box dropped 520 190 440 140 "capture=drop" "The output goes nowhere. It differs" "on every machine, so the page is" "not allowed to quote it. So what is" "left to check?"

note rule 40 390 440 170 "The rule with teeth, over on the" "right hand side: a dropped block" "with nothing asserted about it is" "refused. It was the one place in a" "lesson where a program could print" "anything at all, or stop printing," "and nobody would find out."

box asserts 520 390 440 170 "asserts.json, which is the answer" "This many lines. Contains this." "Does not contain that. A line" "matching this pattern. Each one" "with a reason, checked everywhere," "and printed onto the page."

arrow run stored "pinned"
arrow run dropped "not pinned"
arrow dropped asserts "still checked"

size 1000 590
